  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through Wednesday)\nIssued at 1233 AM CDT Thu Jul 23 2026\n\nLingering moisture from our more active end of the work week may\nsee some isolated storms present Saturday afternoon. However, heat\ncontinues to be the main talking point for the extended period as\nmodel agreement does not see the the upper-level high pressure\nholding over the Panhandles laying off anytime soon. With this\nhigh-pressure in place, the Panhandles will hold onto a more\nstagnate and dry upper-level pattern that will aid in forcing\ntemperatures near or over the triple digit mark clear into the\nmiddle of next. Obviously such hot temperatures over multiple\nconsecutive days rather typical for this time of year. However,\nwhat could make this much more dangerous is that low temperatures\nare not fairing much better with present expectations seeing\nlocations, such as Amarillo, have the potential to either break or\ntie their record warm low temperature each night. Expectations\nlike these would also mean that there is very little relief\noccurring during overnight hours which may only amplify the risk\nof seeing heat related illness as each day passes. Given this\npotential, it is becoming increasingly likely that we will not\nonly see heat related products form much of the period, but also\nhave said products last well into the overnight hours.",
